§6  v06-report re-run at HEAD — EXIT 0, but the intended collapse did NOT happen (premise break)
    Command: node tools/verify/v06-report.cjs
    stdout capture: raw/gates/f61-postcatalog-v06-report-stdout-2026-09-19.log
    Result: status PASS, blockers [], tests {29 suites / 207 tests / 207 passed / success true},
            recipes {catalogTotal 30, validatedCount 30, stableCount 30}, revision.failures [].
    revision.recorded BEFORE this pass: [e06d298, 3a53957]
    revision.recorded AFTER  this pass: [e06d298, 33b4281]     <- the lagging pair rotated, it did not merge
    Reason, measured rather than argued:
      - the dual-track + recipe evidence recorded revision e06d298 and were committed BY 33b4281
        (git log -1 --format=%h -- docs/evidence/v06-recipes.json -> 33b4281 09-19 21:40; same for
        v06-golden-dual-track.json and v06-review-gate.json),
      - a capture can only ever name the HEAD that existed before its own commit, so "committed evidence
        whose recorded revision equals HEAD" is unattainable by construction;
      - git merge-base --is-ancestor e06d298 HEAD -> yes, with 3 commits between e06d298..HEAD.
    Consequence for the two options the user was given:
      (a) re-running ONLY the catalog gate cannot make three sources agree, because my own previous commit
          advanced HEAD. To get a single recorded value all three captures must be re-run at the same HEAD
          (and the value then becomes "one commit behind" again as soon as it is committed - still single).
      (b) asserting recorded == HEAD would emit a permanent, non-actionable warn; the existing invariant
          (ancestor + identical sourceHash + per-run scenarioHash + artifact re-hash) is the correct one
          and it currently reports 0 failures. The real residual is presentation only: revision.recorded is a
          flat de-duplicated list, so a reader cannot tell WHICH input was captured at WHICH revision.
    Recommendation (needs authorization because it touches tools/verify/v06-report.cjs): emit
    revision.perSource = {goldenDualTrack, catalogRuntime, recipeBatch, recipeRuns[]} instead of the flat
    list; keep the ancestor + sourceHash assertions exactly as they are.

